<!doctype html>
<!-- Generated by tools/style-guide.rb. Edit DESIGN.md and tools/style-guide/ instead. -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <meta name="design-source-sha256" content="<%= digest %>">
  <title>CyberShu · style guide</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="data:,">
  <style>
<%= read('tools/style-guide/base.css') %>
<%= css %>
<%= read('tools/style-guide/components.css') %>
  </style>
</head>
<body data-component="page">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="masthead dark">
    <div class="container masthead-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#main" aria-label="CyberShu, start of style guide" data-component="wordmark">Cyber<span data-component="wordmark-accent">Shu</span></a>
      <span class="edition">Visual system / 01</span>
      <a href="DESIGN.md">Documentation ↗</a>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="main" class="container">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Design foundation for the new website</p>
      <h1 data-type="display">Style guide.<br>CyberShu.</h1>
      <div class="intro-bottom"><p>Website identity, reading patterns and interface components for the new CyberShu design.</p><span class="version">DESIGN.md / alpha</span></div>
    </div>
    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Style guide sections">
      <a href="#identity">01 / Identity</a><a href="#colors">02 / Colors</a><a href="#typography">03 / Typography</a><a href="#geometry">04 / Geometry</a><a href="#actions">05 / Actions</a><a href="#forms">06 / Forms</a><a href="#content">07 / Content</a><a href="#states">08 / States</a>
    </nav>

    <details class="coverage"><summary>Coverage against the current website</summary>
      <p>This preview demonstrates the current design baseline. Geometry and component treatments can evolve together; the branding reference does not fix page layouts. It does not yet cover every production page or interaction. The website currently includes a paginated technical blog, tag-filtered archive, consultation offer and English and Polish articles.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Specimen coverage" tabindex="0"><table>
        <caption>Specimens and remaining gaps</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Pattern</th><th scope="col">Coverage</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Brand, tokens and generic controls</th><td>Demonstrated below</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Article body</th><td>Basic prose, lists, code and table; TOC, highlighted code and footer still need specimens</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Blog index and pagination</th><td>Requirements documented; dedicated specimens missing</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Archive filtering and search</th><td>Requirements documented; selected tags, query results and overlay behavior missing</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Consultations and booking</th><td>The local demo form is not the involve.me booking flow; full learning-path and provider specimens missing</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Conference resources</th><td>Download, PDF and Tally feedback-wrapper specimens missing</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">About, Uses and 404</th><td>Page requirements documented; dedicated layouts missing</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
      <p>See the <a href="DESIGN-REVIEW.md">design documentation review</a> and the page-family requirements in <a href="DESIGN.md">DESIGN.md</a>. Brand references supply the palette and updated logo; page composition is designed for the website.</p>
    </details>

    <section id="identity" aria-labelledby="identity-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">01 / Identity</p><h2 id="identity-title" data-type="heading">One identity across the website</h2></div>
      <div class="two-column logo-treatments">
        <div class="panel dark"><p class="eyebrow">Logo on a dark surface</p><p class="brand" data-component="wordmark">Cyber<span data-component="wordmark-accent">Shu</span></p><p data-component="hero-description">Updated wordmark and brand palette.</p></div>
        <div class="panel bordered"><p class="eyebrow">Logo on a reading surface</p><p class="brand" data-type="wordmark">CyberShu</p><p data-component="metadata">Single-color treatment for a light background.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="website-specimen">
        <div class="specimen-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Editorial website specimen</p><a href="#content">Explore article elements ↗</a></div>
        <article class="article-sample">
          <p data-component="metadata">7 September 2026 · Software engineering</p>
          <h3 data-type="heading">Think Before You Build: Side Project Economics in the AI Era</h3>
          <p>A real CyberShu article title used to test the reading hierarchy, line length and metadata treatment of the new website.</p>
          <a href="#content">Read the content specimen ↗</a>
        </article>
        <p class="caption">This demonstrates website identity applied to editorial content. It is not a finalized homepage layout. Profile imagery and promotional introductions are separate, optional page decisions.</p>
      </div>
      <details class="reference"><summary>Brand provenance: palette and logo source</summary><p>The business-card project is a source of updated branding, not a layout template for the website. Print proportions, portrait placement, slogans and QR panels do not prescribe web components.</p><div class="two-column"><img src="design-reference/business-card-v9-front.png" alt="Historical brand reference: business card v9 front" loading="lazy"><img src="design-reference/business-card-v9-back.png" alt="Historical brand reference: business card v9 reverse" loading="lazy"></div></details>
    </section>

    <section id="colors" aria-labelledby="colors-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">02 / Colors</p><h2 id="colors-title" data-type="heading">Navy, cream and an accent</h2></div>
      <div class="swatches">
        <% @tokens.fetch('colors').each do |name, value| %>
        <div class="swatch"><div class="color-sample" style="background-color: var(--colors-<%= h(name) %>)"></div><strong><%= h(name) %></strong><code><%= h(value) %></code></div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="two-column contrast-examples"><div class="panel dark"><p class="eyebrow">On navy</p><p>Cream primary text.</p><p data-component="hero-description">Light gray supporting text.</p><a href="#actions">Orange accent ↗</a></div><div class="panel bordered"><p class="eyebrow">On cream</p><p>Navy primary text.</p><p data-component="metadata">Slate metadata.</p><a href="#actions">Underlined navy link ↗</a></div></div>
      <p class="caption">Orange text belongs on navy. Use navy text on cream.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="typography" aria-labelledby="typography-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">03 / Typography</p><h2 id="typography-title" data-type="heading"><%= h(@tokens.fetch('typography').fetch('body').fetch('fontFamily')) %>. Readable from the first line.</h2></div>
      <p class="caption">Polish character specimen: <span lang="pl">Zażółć gęślą jaźń.</span></p>
      <% @tokens.fetch('typography').each do |name, properties| %>
      <div class="type-row"><div class="type-meta"><code><%= h(name) %></code><span><%= h(properties.fetch('fontSize')) %> / <%= h(properties.fetch('fontWeight')) %> / <%= h(properties.fetch('lineHeight')) %></span></div><p data-type="<%= h(name) %>"><%= name == 'code' ? 'const decision = simplify(problem);' : 'Technology made clear.' %></p></div>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section id="geometry" aria-labelledby="geometry-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">04 / Geometry</p><h2 id="geometry-title" data-type="heading">Space organizes content</h2></div>
      <div class="two-column"><div class="spacing-list">
        <% @tokens.fetch('spacing').each do |name, value| %>
        <div class="spacing-row"><code><%= h(name) %></code><span class="spacing-bar" style="width: var(--spacing-<%= h(name) %>)"></span><span><%= h(value) %></span></div>
        <% end %>
      </div><div class="geometry-notes"><p>Initial geometry: container up to 1200px; article reading column up to 70ch. Validate revised dimensions against real website content.</p><div class="radius-samples"><% @tokens.fetch('rounded').each do |name, value| %><div style="border-radius: var(--rounded-<%= h(name) %>)"><code><%= h(name) %></code><span><%= h(value) %></span></div><% end %></div><p class="caption">Current baseline: flat surfaces. Radii and elevation are adjustable website choices, not print-derived restrictions.</p></div></div>
    </section>

    <section id="actions" aria-labelledby="actions-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">05 / Actions</p><h2 id="actions-title" data-type="heading">Actions with a clear shape</h2></div>
      <div class="action-samples">
        <div><span class="caption">Default</span><button data-component="button-primary" data-demo-action>Primary action</button></div>
        <div><span class="caption">Hover / active</span><button class="button sample-hover" data-component="button-primary-hover" data-demo-action>Primary action</button></div>
        <div><span class="caption">Keyboard focus</span><button class="sample-focus" data-component="button-primary" data-demo-action>Primary action</button></div>
        <div><span class="caption">Secondary</span><button data-component="button-secondary" data-demo-action>More information</button></div>
        <div><span class="caption">Disabled</span><button data-component="button-secondary" disabled>Unavailable</button></div>
        <div><span class="caption">Busy</span><button data-component="button-secondary" disabled aria-busy="true">Saving…</button></div>
      </div>
      <p id="action-status" class="caption status-line" role="status">Examples respond to clicks and the Enter key.</p>
      <div class="panel dark"><p class="eyebrow">On a dark surface</p><div class="button-row"><button data-component="button-primary" data-demo-action>Primary action</button><button data-component="button-secondary" data-demo-action>Secondary action</button><a href="#content">Text link</a></div></div>
      <nav class="demo-navigation" aria-label="Example navigation"><a href="#content" aria-current="page">Articles</a><a href="#forms">Consultations</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>
    </section>

    <section id="forms" aria-labelledby="forms-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">06 / Forms</p><h2 id="forms-title" data-type="heading">Label, field, feedback</h2></div>
      <p>Local demonstration. Data is neither sent nor stored. This is not the production booking form.</p>
      <form id="demo-form" novalidate>
        <div class="two-column"><div class="field"><label for="demo-name">Name</label><input data-component="input" id="demo-name" name="name" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. Alex"></div><div class="field"><label for="demo-email">Email (required)</label><input data-component="input" id="demo-email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="email-help email-error" placeholder="name@example.com"><small id="email-help">This field only demonstrates validation.</small><p id="email-error" class="field-error" hidden></p></div></div>
        <div class="two-column"><div class="field"><label for="demo-topic">Conversation topic</label><select data-component="input" id="demo-topic"><option>Technology decision</option>Business process</option>Product development</option></select></div><div class="field"><label for="demo-disabled">Disabled field</label><input data-component="input" id="demo-disabled" value="Editing unavailable" disabled></div></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="demo-message">Context</label><textarea data-component="input" id="demo-message" rows="3" placeholder="Which problem needs to be solved?"></textarea></div>
        <div class="two-column"><fieldset><legend>Meeting format</legend><label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="meeting" value="online" checked> Online</label><label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="meeting" value="onsite"> In person</label></fieldset><fieldset><legend>Supporting material</legend><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" checked> I have a problem description</label><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox"> I have sample data</label></fieldset></div>
        <div class="button-row"><button type="submit" data-component="button-primary">Validate form</button><button type="reset" data-component="button-secondary">Reset</button></div>
        <p id="form-status" class="status-line" role="status"></p>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section id="content" aria-labelledby="content-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">07 / Content</p><h2 id="content-title" data-type="heading">Room for longer reading</h2></div>
      <div class="editorial-layout"><article class="article-sample"><p class="eyebrow">Example article</p><h3 data-type="subheading">The problem before the tool</h3><p data-component="metadata">Michał Mazur · 26 September 2026 · 4 min read</p><p>Changing a tool can be part of the solution. Start with the process and the decision that needs to be made. <a href="#forms">A short conversation</a> can establish the scope.</p><blockquote><p>Start with the problem and the constraints before choosing an implementation.</p></blockquote><h4>Before the conversation</h4><ul><li>A description of the problem and its effects.</li><li>An example from everyday work.</li></ul><h4>Working through the problem</h4><ol><li>Define the expected outcome.</li><li>Compare the available approaches.</li><li>Test the selected approach.</li></ol><dl><dt>Context</dt><dd>The conditions in which the problem occurs.</dd><dt>Constraint</dt><dd>A resource or requirement that affects the choice.</dd></dl><pre data-component="code-block" tabindex="0" aria-label="Code example"><code>const problem = "Repetitive work";
const result = simplify(problem);
console.log(result);</code></pre></article><aside class="panel bordered"><p class="eyebrow">Supporting panel</p><h3 data-type="subheading">IT consultation</h3><p>Space for a service description, scope or information related to the article.</p><a href="#contact">Go to contact ↗</a><hr data-component="divider-decorative"><div class="tags"><span>Automation</span><span>IT decisions</span></div></aside></div>
      <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Component comparison" tabindex="0"><table><caption>Elements and their use</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Element</th><th scope="col">Use</th><th scope="col">Shape</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Panel</th><td>Group related content</td><td>Rectangle</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Button</th><td>Trigger an action</td><td>4px radius</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Link</th><td>Navigate to content</td><td>Underline</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <details><summary>Expandable information</summary><p>The content is keyboard accessible. Enter or Space opens and closes this element.</p></details>
    </section>

    <section id="states" aria-labelledby="states-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="index">08 / States</p><h2 id="states-title" data-type="heading">The interface explains its state</h2></div>
      <div class="two-column"><div class="notice"><h3>Information</h3><p>Changes in this preview remain local.</p></div><div class="notice"><h3>Success</h3><p>The example operation has completed.</p></div><div class="notice notice-error"><h3>Error</h3><p>The operation could not be completed. Try again.</p></div><div class="notice"><h3>No results</h3><p>Change the query or remove a filter.</p></div></div>
      <div class="panel bordered loading-demo"><label for="demo-progress">Example processing</label><progress id="demo-progress" max="100" value="0">0%</progress><p id="progress-status" role="status">Ready to start.</p><button id="run-progress" data-component="button-secondary">Run example</button></div>
      <button id="open-dialog" data-component="button-secondary">Open example dialog</button>
      <dialog id="demo-dialog" aria-labelledby="dialog-title"><h2 id="dialog-title" data-type="subheading">Example dialog</h2><p>Focus stays within the dialog. Escape closes it and restores focus to the trigger.</p><form method="dialog"><button data-component="button-primary" autofocus>Close</button></form></dialog>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="contact panel dark" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><p class="eyebrow">Contact</p><h2 id="contact-title" data-type="heading">Start a conversation.</h2><a class="contact-address" href="mailto:kontakt@cybershu.eu">kontakt@cybershu.eu</a><a href="https://cybershu.eu">cybershu.eu ↗</a></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="container footer"><p>CyberShu / style guide</p><p>Source: <a href="DESIGN.md">DESIGN.md</a> · <a href="design-reference/fonts/LICENSE.txt">Inter license</a></p><details><summary>Updating the preview</summary><p>Generate tokens and specimens with <code>pnpm style-guide:build</code>. Use <code>pnpm style-guide:watch</code> to regenerate the file after source changes; refresh the browser to see the result. Freshness check: <code>pnpm style-guide:check</code>.</p><p class="caption">Source fingerprint: <code><%= digest[0, 12] %></code>. These specimens do not implement changes on the production website.</p></details></footer>
  <script><%= read('tools/style-guide/interactions.js') %></script>
</body>
</html>
